Z||000000||FIERO1985||11-21-2001||10:14 PM||||What is everyones opinion....A 2.8L build up and mod it out with a turbo? or drop a 5.7L... Not planning on a swap realitively soon but just want everyones view... I know V8s canbe a pain in the ass but the 2.8L can probably be modded well....Let me know what you all think<P>-Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||11-21-2001||10:43 PM||||How is the SBC a pain in the butt?<P> It is the most successful engine GM ( probably any car manufacturer) ever built.<P> It is almost bullet proof, and still today, one of the easiest / cheapest / simplest engines to mod.<P> The power potential of the SBC is almost limitless.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||11-22-2001||12:57 AM||||bolt in a 3.4 pushrod and add turbo.  :cool||||reg||1
Z||000003||rgeeinc||11-22-2001||02:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIERO1985:<BR><B>What is everyones opinion....A 2.8L build up and mod it out with a turbo? or drop a 5.7L...   <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you are really going to do one or the other, you really need to ask your self a few questions. First how fast do you really want to go, how are you going to drive this car, and what are you willing to spend to do all this. Then you need to do your homework, and I don't mean just reading the post on PFF<BR>Having had both a turbo 2.8 V6 and a V8, there is no question about witch one to do.<BR>For me it's the V8. They are not a pain in the ass as you put it, but you really need to think about how much build up you are going to do in the 2.8 V6 BEFORE adding the turbo. If you want the motor to last. Then make your informed decision, and go from there. Good Luck<P>Bob... 85 GT ZZ4 Corson Kit||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroX||11-22-2001||06:39 PM||||is the 3800 series II supercharged out of the question?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIERO1985||11-22-2001||07:10 PM||||pretty much I want to be able to service this car (85gt) easily. Not harder than the 2.8L is at least I know other parts of the car will hold up longer with less power...<P>Lets picture a stock 5.7L with 300hp (for instance)<P>Then a 2.8L stroked to a 3.1L larger throttle body. Turbo, headers, full exhaust, the engine with the stroker kit along with a larger cam and some head and valve work can put out 200hp and with a turbo,exhaust and a TB then we can look at with some other mods around 270hp maybe which will be pretty damn quick considering the 140 hp now?<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||11-22-2001||08:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIERO1985:<BR><B>pretty much I want to be able to service this car (85gt) easily. Not harder than the 2.8L is at least I know other parts of the car will hold up longer with less power...<P>Lets picture a stock 5.7L with 300hp (for instance)<P>Then a 2.8L stroked to a 3.1L larger throttle body. Turbo, headers, full exhaust, the engine with the stroker kit along with a larger cam and some head and valve work can put out 200hp and with a turbo,exhaust and a TB then we can look at with some other mods around 270hp maybe which will be pretty damn quick considering the 140 hp now?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not trying to sway you from a V6 Turbo, but you seem to have alot of down falls on the V8 Fiero.<BR> Why did you ask this question in the first place if you think the V8 is a terrible thing in the Fiero.<P> The V8 is easier to work at / service in the Fiero than the 2.8. Do a search on some posts by Archie, he's got the proof there in pictures.<P> By all means if you want a turbo V6, go for it! but you forgot something....TORQUE<P> Read rgeeinc's post again, theres a person that knows.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||11-23-2001||04:16 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> <P>Love that image!!!  (please tell me the needle rests there sans-power, please! Eeeeek!)<P><BR>Anyway, the SBC in a Fiero is easier to work on than a 2.8...<P>It's a very tried and true swap, with as near perfect a record as ANY engine swap I've EVER seen into any car...<P>'How fast do you want to go?'<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
